android/maxima-core/ is the shared core of the Maxima transport, vendored from
https://github.com/eurobuddha/maxima at commit 6e001754428623b891bc582b05fe505c1f96f37c
(its core/src/main tree, unmodified: 88 files, checked byte for byte against
that commit on 2026-09-22). It is what makes this app a Maxima node rather than
an app asking another app to be one for it. Java 11, no runtime dependencies.

Copyright (c) 2026 eurobuddha. It is under the MIT License, whose full text is
in android/maxima-core/LICENSE (copied from that repository at commit
6c71fbfde539419bf06fe4e096aa9209fbad72a9, "License original Maxima and Parlons
code under MIT", 2026-10-31), and is packed into every build beside the code as
MAXIMA-LICENSE.txt. Its author confirmed to this project's owner, on 2026-11-02,
that the licence covers the commit vendored here. It is not under this
project's LICENSE, and the GPL is not put on it.

Before that licence existed, the author was asked, on 2026-09-21, whether
Mininotes may be published with this tree inside it and credited to them, and
answered on 2026-09-22: "go for it", "with my blessing". That permission is
kept here as history; the MIT License now governs the tree. The same credit is
beside the code, in android/maxima-core/NOTICE. See docs/MAXIMA-TRANSPORT.md.

SHA3-256 is not vendored: Android provides none at any version, and rather than
take a cryptography library for one function, org.mininotes.android.Sha3 is an
implementation of Keccak-f[1600] checked against the published NIST answers.

